       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 2400 mg per dose four times daily comes to **9,600 mg/day**. The maximum for an adult is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single 2400 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg. That much ibuprofen risks GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day total\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day total\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**, which is 1,600 mg/day total\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2400 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also like to add a note with the clinical rationale."
